-- title:
--   There are fifty $Γ_H(25)$–$⟨ST⟩$ double cosets
-- statement:
--   Let $Γ=Γ_H(25)≤SL_2(ℤ)$ for $H=H_{25}$, and let $S,T$ be the standard modular generators. The double-coset space for $Γ$ and the cyclic subgroup generated by $ST$ has cardinality $$|Γ\backslash SL_2(ℤ)/⟨ST⟩|=50.$$ This is the order-three elliptic-orbit count entering the finite level-$25$ census.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

